For accessibility I'm dropping this into our global stylesheet:

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation: none !important;
    transition: none !important;
  }
}
```

That covers the whole app in one shot, right? For context the app has a hero with a looping ambient gradient, a bottom sheet the user drags with their finger, and status chips that currently crossfade between colours when a job changes state.
